msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/dpll.rst:232
msgid ""
"nested attribute for requesting configuration on given parent dpll device"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/dpll.rst:236 ../../../driver-api/dpll.rst:460
msgid "``DPLL_A_PIN_PHASE_OFFSET``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/dpll.rst:236
msgid "attr measured phase difference between a pin and parent dpll device"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/dpll.rst:240
msgid ""
"All phase related values are provided in pico seconds, which represents time "
"difference between signals phase. The negative value means that phase of "
"signal on pin is earlier in time than dpll's signal. Positive value means "
"that phase of signal on pin is later in time than signal of a dpll."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/dpll.rst:246
msgid ""
"Phase adjust (also min and max) values are integers, but measured phase "
"offset values are fractional with 3-digit decimal places and shell be "
"divided with ``DPLL_PIN_PHASE_OFFSET_DIVIDER`` to get integer part and "
"modulo divided to get fractional part."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/dpll.rst:252
msgid "Phase offset monitor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/dpll.rst:254
msgid ""
"Phase offset measurement is typically performed against the current active "
"source. However, some DPLL (Digital Phase-Locked Loop) devices may offer the "
"capability to monitor phase offsets across all available inputs. The "
"attribute and current feature state shall be included in the response "
"message of the ``DPLL_CMD_DEVICE_GET`` command for supported DPLL devices. "
"In such cases, users can also control the feature using the "
"``DPLL_CMD_DEVICE_SET`` command by setting the ``enum dpll_feature_state`` "
"values for the attribute. Once enabled the phase offset measurements for the "
"input shall be returned in the ``DPLL_A_PIN_PHASE_OFFSET`` attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/dpll.rst:266
msgid "``DPLL_A_PHASE_OFFSET_MONITOR``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/dpll.rst:266 ../../../driver-api/dpll.rst:304
msgid "attr state of a feature"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/dpll.rst:270
msgid "Fractional frequency offset"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/dpll.rst:272
msgid ""
"The fractional frequency offset (FFO) is reported through two attributes "
"that carry the same measurement at different precisions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/dpll.rst:275
msgid "``DPLL_A_PIN_FRACTIONAL_FREQUENCY_OFFSET`` in PPM (parts per million)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/dpll.rst:276
msgid ""
"``DPLL_A_PIN_FRACTIONAL_FREQUENCY_OFFSET_PPT`` in PPT (parts per trillion)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/dpll.rst:278
msgid ""
"Both attributes appear at the top level of a pin and inside each ``pin-"
"parent-device`` nest. Two FFO types are defined:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/dpll.rst:281
msgid "``DPLL_FFO_PORT_RXTX_RATE`` - RX vs TX symbol rate offset (top-level)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/dpll.rst:282
msgid "``DPLL_FFO_PIN_DEVICE`` - pin vs parent DPLL offset (per-parent)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/dpll.rst:284
msgid ""
"The driver declares which types it supports via the ``supported_ffo`` "
"bitmask in ``struct dpll_pin_ops``. The core only calls the ``ffo_get`` "
"callback for types the driver has opted into. The requested type is passed "
"to the driver in the ``struct dpll_ffo_param``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/dpll.rst:290
msgid "Frequency monitor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/dpll.rst:292
msgid ""
"Some DPLL devices may offer the capability to measure the actual frequency "
"of all available input pins. The attribute and current feature state shall "
"be included in the response message of the ``DPLL_CMD_DEVICE_GET`` command "
"for supported DPLL devices. In such cases, users can also control the "
"feature using the ``DPLL_CMD_DEVICE_SET`` command by setting the ``enum "
"dpll_feature_state`` values for the attribute. Once enabled the measured "
"input frequency for each input pin shall be returned in the "
"``DPLL_A_PIN_MEASURED_FREQUENCY`` attribute. The value is in millihertz "
"(mHz), using ``DPLL_PIN_MEASURED_FREQUENCY_DIVIDER`` as the divider."
msgstr ""

